          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong framed link
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/link"} link
            where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circles"} circles
            forming the components are viewed as having a thickness, albeit an arbitrarily small thickness. That is to say, instead of the components of the links being
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+smooth+manifolds"} embedded
            circles, they are embedded solid
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tori"} tori
          %p
            The thickening can be considered in one direction only which gives
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+smooth+manifolds"} embedded
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ribbons"} ribbons
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dehn+twist"} Dehn twist
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/link+diagram"} link diagram
            can be made into a diagram of a framed links by giving it the
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong blackboard framing
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The precise notion of a framing on a link is perhaps most naturally given in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth structures
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
          %h3#framing Framing
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} oriented
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-manifold"} 3-manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p: T M \to M
            is a bundle with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+group"} structure group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(3) = GL(\mathbb{R}^3)
            which in fact admits a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+of+the+structure+group"} reduction
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_+(3)
            (invertible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+transformations"} linear transformations
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant"} determinant
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is oriented. A further reduction to the structure group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%283%29"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(3)
            can be effected by a number of means, e.g., by equipping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            with a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
          %p Now let
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⊔
                  %mi …
                  %mo ⊔
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  L
                  \\;\colon\;
                  S^1 \sqcup \ldots \sqcup S^1 \hookrightarrow M
          %p
            be a smoothly embedded link (of oriented circles). The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+bundle"} normal bundle
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            of the bundle inclusion
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⊔
                  %mi …
                  %mo ⊔
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mo *
                  %mi T
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(S^1 \sqcup \ldots \sqcup S^1) \to L^\ast T M
          %p
            (as bundles over
            = succeed ");" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi …
                    %mo ⊔
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1 \sqcup \ldots \sqcup S^1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal
            = succeed "-bundle." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(2)
            %em framing
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is simply a choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            of this principal
            = succeed "-bundle." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(2)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            can be seen as an embedded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\xi, p)
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in S^1
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\sigma(p)\xi, p)
          %h3#framing_number Framing number
          %p
            However, it is often convenient to consider such framings, or rather their associated torus
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphisms"} diffeomorphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isotopy"} isotopy
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isotopy+class"} isotopy class
            is specified by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
            which gives the number of 360 degree clockwise rotations of the unit normal or clockwise twists of the ribbon as one traverses the component in the direction of its orientation. This is called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em framing number
          %p
            If one regards the framed link as a ribbon link, then its framing number is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linking+number"} linking number
            of the two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+of+a+manifold"} boundaries
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ribbon"} ribbon
          %p
            Thus an alternative way of describing a framing on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oriented+link"} oriented link
            is by assigning an integer (framing number) to each link component.
          %p
          #LinkingMatrix.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              The
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linking+matrix"} linking matrix
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framed+link"} framed link
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/square+matrix"} square matrix
              indexed by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
              of the link whose off-diagonal entries are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linking+numbers"} linking numbers
              and whose diagonal entries are the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framing+numbers"} framing numbers
          (e.g.
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#Ohtsuki01"} Ohtsuki 2001 p 227
          %p
            Notice that the linking matrix is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+matrix"} symmetric matrix
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            Framings of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trefoil+knot"} trefoil knot
          %div{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/FramingsOfTrefoilKnot.jpg", :width => "700px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                From
                %a{:href => "#CMNP19"} CMNP 19
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#ReidemeisterMoves Reidemeister moves
          %p
            A pair of framed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/link+diagrams"} link diagrams
            corresponds to the same framed link iff they may be deformed into each other by diagram
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isotopies"} isotopies
            and the following versions of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reidemeister+moves"} Reidemeister moves
            (e.g.
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#Ohtsuki01"} Ohtsuki 2001 Thm. 1.8
          %div{:style => "margin: -30px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/FramedLinkReidemeister-240718.jpg", :width => "650px"}/
          %p
